Z||000000||Fiero_24||12-23-2001||11:30 PM||||All I can say is WOW!  What a big difference in the new motor with all the performance mods.  Now I just have to figure out my oil pressure problem and take it in to have roller rockers added.  I now have 10 miles on my new motor, too bad the roads were bad.  If you want any info on my mods check my site out.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||12-23-2001||11:37 PM||||CONGRATS! I knew it would all work out in the end for you. I'm glad to hear that she's driving good and especially glad that you're happy with it! It is to bad that the roads are as bad as they are today though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Now, more importantly, when do i get a ride?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000002||Fiero_24||12-23-2001||11:47 PM||||Soon Dave.  You will like how quick this car is.  First I have to fix the oil pressure problem and have the roller rockers put in.  I thought I had the rockers adjusted right, but they are still loud.  I refuse to take the top end off that car again, so I am going to have my mechanic put the rollers on for me since they have to open the motor up anyway.  I am haveing a shift kit put in the tranny too.  Over all I am very happy.  What a nice early Christmas present, huh?||||reg||7
